{"id":"diagram-revision-d63d6047-ce29-463e-a4fe-915f20f7d620","diagramId":"diagram-5d2bc009-df74-4f64-a3d4-75d756b9582f","parentId":"diagram-revision-a849b15f-57a6-426b-92dc-62e17d22034e","diagram":{"id":"overview","revision":2,"diagramId":"diagram-5d2bc009-df74-4f64-a3d4-75d756b9582f","revisionId":"diagram-revision-d63d6047-ce29-463e-a4fe-915f20f7d620","content":{"revisionId":"overview:2","ascii":"Saved CanvasViews and branching\n|\n+-- Give the current canvas a durable name\n|   +-- Create a view: save immediately and make it the active view\n|   |   `-- CanvasHistory.canvasView({ operation: 'create', name })\n|   `-- A saved checkpoint preserves the canvas and its exact diagram revisions\n|       +-- Earlier checkpoints remain immutable when you save again\n|       `-- CanvasView: startCheckpointId / checkpointIds / finalCheckpointId\n|\n+-- Continue working within a view\n|   +-- Edit freely: the current canvas can diverge from its saved checkpoint\n|   |   `-- The unsaved indicator ignores camera and selection-only changes\n|   +-- Save when this state should become the new starting point\n|   |   +-- Save view or Ctrl+S updates the active view's saved endpoint\n|   |   `-- operation: 'save' -> retain checkpoints; clear its workingCopies entry\n|   `-- Leave and return without losing unfinished work\n|       +-- Opening another view stashes the outgoing view's current state\n|       |   `-- stashCanvasView() -> workingCopies[activeViewId] = headId\n|       `-- Reopen the target view with the current camera kept in place\n|           +-- Working copy exists: resume its unsaved edits\n|           +-- No working copy: restore its latest saved checkpoint\n|           `-- openCanvasView() -> workingCopies[viewId] ?? finalCheckpointId\n|\n`-- Explore independent branches from a saved starting point\n    +-- Save the parent first if its unfinished edits belong in the branches\n    |   `-- Forking uses the last saved checkpoint, excluding unsaved edits\n    +-- Choose how many directions to explore\n    |   +-- Fork one child: create it and open it immediately\n    |   |   `-- operation: 'fork', viewId, name\n    |   `-- Create an alternative group: independent siblings from ONE checkpoint\n    |       +-- The parent canvas stays open; these are initial copies\n    |       `-- operation: 'alternatives', viewId, names\n    +-- Each branch remembers where it came from\n    |   +-- parentViewId names the parent; forkCheckpointId pins its saved state\n    |   `-- Example ancestry: a saved design\n    |       +-- Spacious layout: one child, independently edited and saved\n    |       |   `-- Spacious with notes: a further fork belongs below this child\n    |       `-- Compact layout: a sibling, independently edited and saved\n    |           `-- alternativeGroupId groups candidates from the same choice\n    `-- Decide which direction to retain\n        +-- Keep a chosen alternative: open or resume it, then save it\n        |   +-- Its own descendants remain available\n        |   `-- Archive the other members of its group\n        |       `-- Also archive every descendant of those other members\n        +-- Discard a view: archive that branch and all its descendants\n        |   `-- If this removes the active branch\n        |       +-- Open the discarded view's parent when it is available\n        |       `-- Otherwise retain the canvas and clear the active view\n        `-- Archiving hides branches from the explorer; saved history remains\n            `-- archivedAt marks hidden views; ancestry and checkpoints persist","asciiSha256":"9389b6eb7a538ea10099277570c5fcc0c54e064f28ca776fcac1ae36c6c92099","structure":{"kind":"tree","parserVersion":"ascii-tree-2","rootIds":["overview:2:9389b6eb7a538ea10099277570c5fcc0c54e064f28ca776fcac1ae36c6c92099:line-1"],"nodes":{"overview:2:9389b6eb7a538ea10099277570c5fcc0c54e064f28ca776fcac1ae36c6c92099:line-1":{"id":"overview:2:9389b6eb7a538ea10099277570c5fcc0c54e064f28ca776fcac1ae36c6c92099:line-1",